course: dictionary
lesson: 7325
title: Plan: an idea, a drawing, or a decision
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word plan has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. «Our plan is to leave at nine.» Here a plan is an idea of what you will do and how.
explain: «A floor plan» is a drawing of a building seen from above, like a map of the rooms. Ask yourself: is the plan a thing you look at, or something you think about?
explain: As a verb, plan is a doing word. «Plan a party» means to decide and organise what to do. Try the swap test: "decide and organise" fits the sentence, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Plan can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (a doing word).
fact: «Plan» as a noun means an idea of what you will do and how.
fact: A plan view is a drawing of something seen from above, like a map.
fact: «Planned» means decided and organised ahead of time, as in «weekend clubs and planned visits help».
fact: Useful phrases: «make a plan», «plan ahead», and «plan B», which is a second choice if the first one fails.
exercise: «Our plan is to leave at nine.» What does plan mean here? | A kind of cake | A drawing of a building from above | To hit something hard | *An idea of what you will do and how
exercise: In maths, what is a plan view? | *A drawing of something seen from above | A story about a fish | A long sum with many steps | A view from the side
exercise: «Plan a party» uses plan as which kind of word? | An adjective | A full stop | *A verb | A noun
test: «A surprise is being planned, and it is kinder not to go looking for it.» What does planned mean? | Shouted about | *Arranged and decided ahead | Lost | Broken
test: What does plan B mean? | A map of the moon | Plan A, but louder | The second page of a book | *A second choice if the first plan does not work
exam: «In an emergency there is no time to chat: it is better to know your fire plan by heart.» What is a fire plan? | *What you will do and how, if there is a fire | A type of fire extinguisher | A drawing of a fire engine | A song about fire
